After collecting a gargantuan pile (>200 items) on the first level of
Gehennom, I decided to do a little polypiling.  There were a lot of stones
in the pile from when I had a cockatrice corpse, so I figured I'd get lucky
and get a lot of gems.  First pile was great--73 dilithium crystals and
16 amber stones.  A couple shots later I was getting tired of paging thru
all those pages of items, so after polypiling again I simply went and
picked up all the gems in the pile.  Big mistake.

g  5 topaz stones
m  6 turquoise stones
t  113 loadstones

AAAIIIIIEEEEEEEEE!!!!!!!!  My bag of holding with a dozen holy waters was
but one square away.  Unfortunately I was not just Overtaxed, but Overloaded.
That means you can't do much of anything, never mind moving.  Since I was in
Gehennom I couldn't pray, either.
*Sigh.*  Slow deaths still exist in 3.1.
